{
  "dom_id": "step-e8052",
  "name": "Example: Solving Equations With Even Exponents",
  "problem": "Find all of the real solutions to the equation $9x^4 = \\dfrac{1}{9}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by isolating the $x^4$ term and then taking the $4$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $x^4$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ {x}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{81}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $4$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since the exponent $(4)$ is even, we consider both the positive and negative solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{81} \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{{x}^{4}} & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{\\frac{1}{81}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\dfrac13.$",
